sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor U as User
    participant UI as Streamlit Dashboard
    participant RG as ReportGenerator.py
    participant DBM as DBManager.py
    participant DB as Postgres (clean/analytics)

    Note over U, DB: User wants to see market insights

    U->>UI: Select Data Target (e.g. "Kraków - Sale")
    
    par Load Market Trends (Macro)
        UI->>DBM: get_batch_metrics(criteria_id)
        DBM->>DB: SELECT metrics, calculated_at FROM analytics.batch_metrics WHERE criteria_id = N
        DB-->>DBM: JSONB data (AVG, Median, Supply)
        DBM->>DBM: Flatten JSON to Pandas DataFrame
    and Load Current Anomalies (Micro)
        UI->>DBM: get_latest_anomalies(criteria_id, read_only_new)
        DBM->>DB: SELECT * FROM analytics.detected_anomalies WHERE criteria_id = N
        DB-->>DBM: List of anomalies + listing_snapshots
    end

    DBM-->>UI: Structured Data for Charts & Tables

    Note over UI: Data Processing (Pandas/Plotly)
    UI->>UI: Generate Charts
    UI->>UI: Generate Anomaly List
    
    UI-->>U: Display Interactive Dashboard
    
    U->>UI: Click "Mark as Read" on an anomaly
    UI->>DBM: update_anomaly_status(anomaly_id)
    DBM->>DB: UPDATE detected_anomalies SET is_read = true WHERE id = N
    DB-->>UI: OK
    UI-->>U: Anomaly disappears from "New" list

    Note over U, DB: User wants a portable PDF report

    U->>UI: Click "Generate PDF Report"
    UI->>RG: trigger_report_generation(criteria_id)
    
    RG->>DBM: get_report_data(criteria_id)
    DBM->>DB: SELECT recent anomalies & batch metrics
    DB-->>DBM: Data result set
    DBM-->>RG: Structured Data (DataFrames)
    
    RG->>RG: Generate Charts (Plotly/Matplotlib)
    RG->>RG: Format PDF Layout (Header, Tables, Charts)
    
    RG-->>UI: PDF Byte Stream
    UI-->>U: Trigger Browser Download (report.pdf)